<Base title="How the Vault Guide handles safety — Vault Human" description="The Vault Guide is an AI guide, not a person and not therapy. Here is how it handles safety.">
  <div class="wrap" style="max-width:720px;padding:48px 20px">
    <h1>How the Vault Guide handles safety</h1>
    <p>The "Find your Key" guide on this site is <b>Russ's AI guide, not Russ</b>, and it is labeled as AI on every screen. Vault Human is coaching, not therapy. The guide never diagnoses, treats or counsels, and it gives no medical, legal or financial advice.</p>
    <h2>If you are in crisis</h2>
    <p>If anything you write suggests thoughts of suicide or self-harm, abuse, or that you or someone else is in danger, the guide stops right away and shows this message:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Call or text <a href="tel:988">988</a>, the Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline (free, any time, in the U.S.), or chat at <a href="https://988lifeline.org/">988lifeline.org</a>.</li>
      <li>If you or someone else is in immediate danger, call <a href="tel:911">911</a>.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Fixed word rules check every message first, and the AI is a second check. The conversation then ends. Nothing is saved and nobody is alerted: we never promise live monitoring we can't give.</p>
    <h2>Adults only</h2>
    <p>The guide is for people 18 and over. If someone tells it they're younger, it stops and points them to a parent, a school counselor or 988.</p>
    <h2>Your words</h2>
    <p>What you type goes to our AI provider to write a reply, and isn't saved unless you tap "Send this to Russ." If you do, he reads it before your call. We never sell it or use it to train AI, and we'll delete it if you ask: <a href="mailto:vault@vaulthuman.com">vault@vaulthuman.com</a>. The guide runs no ad pixels or trackers, and nothing you type is used for advertising.</p>
    <p>Questions about this page: <a href="mailto:vault@vaulthuman.com">vault@vaulthuman.com</a> · (888) 833-2510.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
